<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maio of Bari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1160</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maio of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> was the chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-sicily">William I of Sicily</a>, holding the title emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> from 1154. The son of a judge of Bari, he dominated the royal government and was hated by the barons, who blamed him for the loss of the North African territories to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>. He was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> on 10 November 1160 by conspirators led by Matthew Bonellus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maio-of-bari.jpg" alt="Maio of Bari" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bjs · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palermo-San-Cataldo-bjs-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
